title: 'fix(pallet-broker): Make benchmarks PriceAdapter-agnostic'
doc:
- audience: Runtime Dev
  description: |
    The `pallet-broker` benchmarks previously hard-coded the price computation of
    the `Linear` price adapter (via a `get_start_end_price` helper that called
    `leadin_factor_at` and `adapt_price` directly). This caused the benchmark
    assertions to fail for runtimes configured with a different `PriceAdapter`
    implementation. The benchmarks now derive the expected sale prices from the
    actual `SaleInfo` produced by `do_start_sales`, using `Pallet::sale_price`,
    so they are correct for any `PriceAdapter`. This only touches benchmarking
    code gated behind the `runtime-benchmarks` feature; runtime behaviour is
    unchanged.
crates:
- name: pallet-broker
  bump: none
